<title>ISRAEL: Israel's November trade deficit $526 million.</title>
<headline>Israel's November trade deficit $526 million.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's trade deficit in November totalled $526 million, the Central Bureau of Statistics said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>		     Nov 96   Oct 96   Nov 95</p>
<p>Exports	    1,711    1,766    1,713</p>
<p>Imports	    2,237    2,648    2,499</p>
<p>Balance		526	883	787</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>In the first 11 months of the year the deficit totalled $9.558 billion, up 4.3 percent from the same period last year. The bureau said that since the second quarter, there has been a consistent declining trend in imports against rising exports.</p>
<p>- Jerusalem newsroom, 972-3-537-0502</p>
</text>
